    "background_story": "Itzel was a mysterious and alluring figure in the city's underground art scene. Her style was a fusion of vintage elegance and modern decadence, often turning heads with her bold fashion choices. By day, she worked as a curator at a local gallery, but by night, she transformed into a sultry chanteuse, performing at secret speakeasies and hidden cabarets. Itzel's louche reputation preceded her, with whispers of her scandalous affairs and outrageous antics spreading like wildfire. Yet, those who knew her understood that beneath her provocative exterior lay a sharp intellect and a passion for artistic innovation. Itzel's life was a constant balancing act between creativity and excess, but she wouldn't have it any other way.",
